# Purpose: Pin line endings that interpreters depend on, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# A POSIX shell reads a CR as part of the word: a CRLF checkout turns `set -eu`
# into `set -eu\r`. src/wsl/package_update.sh is embedded with include_str!,
# which copies the file byte for byte (unlike a string literal, whose CRLF rustc
# normalizes), and WSL runs it with `sh -lc`. A Python entry point breaks the
# same way: with a CR after `#!/usr/bin/env python3`, env looks for "python3\r".
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
scripts/pre-commit text eol=lf
